{:edb/db-before-t 2172 :edb/db-after-t 2173 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535485 50 #inst "2026-10-09T01:01:33.944Z" 13194139535485 true] [17592186064198 1020 #edb/ref 17592186351578 13194139535485 true] [17592186064198 1020 #edb/ref 17592186351592 13194139535485 true] [17592186064198 1020 #edb/ref 17592186351600 13194139535485 true] [17592186064199 1020 #edb/ref 17592186351585 13194139535485 true] [17592186064392 1017 #edb/ref 17592186061036 13194139535485 false] [17592186064392 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351572 13194139535485 true] [17592186064392 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535485 true] [17592186064392 1100 "Express the Maclaurin series expansion for $\\frac{1}{1 - x}$, given by\n\n$\\frac{1}{1 - x} = 1 + x + x^{2} + x^{3} + ⋯, x ∈ (-1, 1)$\nusing sigma notation." 13194139535485 false] [17592186064392 1100 "Express the Maclaurin series expansion for $\\frac{1}{1-x},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{1-x}=1+x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+⋯\\,,\\,x\\in (-1,1)\n$$\n\nusing sigma notation." 13194139535485 true] [17592186064392 1145 "The first four terms of the series are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =1 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =x \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can express these terms using a common format, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={x}^{0} \\\\ {a}_{1} & ={x}^{1} \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe deduce that the general formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={x}^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-x} & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{x}^{n}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535485 true] [17592186351572 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351573 13194139535485 true] [17592186351572 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351574 13194139535485 true] [17592186351572 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351575 13194139535485 true] [17592186351572 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351576 13194139535485 true] [17592186351572 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351577 13194139535485 true] [17592186351572 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13